[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-integration-bug-trial-3[0m[0m
All three bugs are fixed. Here's a summary of the changes and why they work:

**The Bug**: A classic TOCTOU (Time-Of-Check-Time-Of-Use) race. The old code did `check_stock` → `charge` → `decrement` as three separate operations. Between `check_stock` returning True and `decrement` running, another concurrent order could steal the last item. The payment was already made — ghost charge.

| File | Change | Fixes |
|------|--------|-------|
| `inventory.py:24-34` | Added `reserve(quantity)` — atomically checks AND decrements stock in one call | TOCTOU race — no window for another coroutine to interleave |
| `inventory.py:36-39` | Added `release(quantity)` — restores stock when payment fails | Leaked inventory |
| `checkout.py:8-25` | New flow: **reserve → charge → release on fail** (replaced `check_stock`+`decrement`) | Ghost charges, overselling |
| `payments.py:9,18-19` | Added `_charged_order_ids` set, idempotent `charge()` | Duplicate charges |

**Why the new flow works**: `reserve` is a single async method that checks stock and subtracts it in one step. No overlap possible — it's one `await`. If the payment fails, `release` puts the stock back. Every charge is guaranteed to have stock allocated before payment runs, and stock is never subtracted without a corresponding charge.
